==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|gibbus||humped, hunched|lang=la}}, probably cognate with {{term/t|la|cubō||bend oneself, lie down}}, Italian {{term|gobba||humpback|lang=it}}, Greek {{term|sc=Grek|κύφος|tr=kyphos||humpback, bent|lang=el}},  {{term|sc=Grek|κύβος|tr=kybos||cube, vertebra|lang=el}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɡɪbəs/}}
* {{rhymes|ɪbəs}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Characterized by [[convex|convexity]]; [[protuberant]].
# {{context|astronomy|lang=en}} Phase of [[moon]] or [[planet]] between first quarter and full or between full and last [[quarter]].
# [[humpback|Humpbacked]].

